      "widgets_values": [
        "WF 2b3 - PANORAMA UPSCALE WITH SEEDVR2 (streamed one trajectory at a time)\n\nSame job as 2b1 (upscale the raw equirect panoramas before SfM) but with SeedVR2\ninstead of the RealESRGAN + Krea2 tile rail, and with the batch numbers wired up\nautomatically instead of set by hand.\n\nRun this FIRST, then 2b2_sfm_from_upscaled_dualres on the same dataset - the output\nfolder panoramas_upscaled/ is exactly what that workflow's hires_dir expects.\n\nWHY THE PLAN NODE EXISTS (the dependency cycle)\nThe obvious wiring - loader -> suggested_batch_size -> Meta Batch Manager -> back into\nthe loader - is a cycle, and ComfyUI refuses it outright:\n    Dependency cycle detected: 30 -> 10 -> 30\nIt has to. The manager cannot be built out of a value produced by the node it drives.\nDataset Upscale Plan sidesteps it by reading the dataset marker straight off disk, so it\ndepends on nothing in the loop and can feed BOTH numbers forward:\n    Plan --frames_per_view------> Meta Batch Manager.frames_per_batch\n         \\-suggested_batch_size--> SeedVR2.batch_size\nSet max_batch_size once to the largest batch your card handles (9 for 7B fp16) and the\nnode always returns a legal value at or below it - 4n+1 AND a divisor of the view length,\nso no internal chunk straddles a boundary. Nothing left to keep in sync by hand.\n\nWHAT A \"VIEW\" IS HERE\nFor panoramas the coherent clip is a TRAJECTORY, not a cube face. The plan node reads\ntrajectory_lengths from the marker (dark-alley: 4 x 81), so frames_per_batch = 81 hands\nSeedVR2 exactly one fly-through per iteration. Panos are named frame_00000.png upward, so\nthe loader's lexical order IS temporal order and each 81-block is one trajectory - which\nis why the plain VHS loader is enough here and no camera-major reordering is needed.\n\nMEMORY, NOT VRAM, IS WHAT KILLED 2b\nThe original 2b tried to hold every upscaled pano in one IMAGE batch. At 8K that is ~32 GB\nper copy and the sharpening stacked it five times - 163 GB. Here each trajectory is\nwritten to disk by the streaming saver and freed before the next one starts.\n\nRESOLUTION: SeedVR2's 'resolution' is the SHORT edge, so on a 2:1 equirect it is the\nHEIGHT. 2048 gives a 4096x2048 pano (preset). 4096 gives the full 8192x4096 the HiRes rail\nwants, but that is 4x the pixels - expect to drop max_batch_size hard, possibly to 1.\nRaise it in steps and watch the console.\n\nThe frames are written under their ORIGINAL filenames, so panoramas_upscaled/ sorts 1:1\nagainst panoramas/ - the ordering 2b2's dual-res SfM relies on.\n\nThe throwaway VHS_VideoCombine is REQUIRED: VideoHelperSuite only keeps a meta-batch loop\nrequeueing while a VHS_VideoCombine sits on the manager. It is fed the cheap low-res\nframes with save_output=false, so it only advances the loop."
      ],
